u can't shoot your  weapons unless you have a pistol as a  secondary and even then the angle feels  like a little odd however it is a pretty  neat way to clamber out of sight and  potentially do some parkour of a  building like a shortcut of sorts it's  balanced by the fact that you have to  get off the ledge to reload the perk  system has been a thing for countless of  past call of duties and a lot of them  like overkill or scavenger reappear in  modern warfare 2 but perks are built out  in packages that you earn over time so  unlike modern warfare 2019 you don't  have to choose between kill streaks and  stacking perks like you did with the  specialist system perks are set up in a  scorestreak system now so the more  points you get the more perks you can  activate so kills assists defending a  capture point and many more tactics will  help you become a more powerful force to  go against one standout perk that i  think everyone should look into at least  early on in the meta is the self revive  as your ultimate perk since combat is so  fast and frenetic it can be easy to  forget to double check that the target  you eliminated is actually dead and not  just down trust me i've had countless  instances where self-revive proved to be  really clutch  there's also other advantages to using  self-revive for one you can potentially  crawl to safety if you're downed at a  distance teammates can revive you  instead and if they choose to do so you  can be revived even faster still need to  test this but if a teammate revives you  i want to say there's still a chance  that you can use your self revive again  if you become down to the same life i  mean what i do know is that if you are  able to pull off a successful self  revive your killstreak count won't be  reset at least until you die again but  all in all it is my personal favorite  ultimate although eagle-eyed players  might prefer one of the other ones i  know there's a perk that gives you a  better mini map for example so it's up  to you some other perk packages to  consider are how each can combine the  different perks to feed off each other  in a synergetic way  so extra tactical and resupply perks  that means you've got throwable gear for  days  a varied arsenal means a deadly arsenal  and you can use gadgets to give you that  extra umph when engaged with enemies let  me start with the funny [ __ ] right off  the bat there is a blow up dummy  it can also kill you  amazing seriously though the blow up  decoy dummy is not a joke and it caught  me off guard several times thinking that  it was a real dude definitely worth  trying out and faking out a couple of  enemies and getting them to fire which  makes them pop up on your radar 2 if  you're clever about it only thing to  consider is that it's one of the few  gadgets with an extremely long recharge  time  pro tip the dummy will always orient  towards an approaching enemy to let you  know where they are coming from there  are some excellent gadgets to keep an  eye out for the trophy system makes its  return and it still stops an airstrike  killstreak like in modern warfare 2019.  seriously i got the receipts right here  there is a personal radar that you can  toss out like a landmine that will ping  enemies in a decent range near your  vicinity and there's even a ddos now the  ddos is my personal favorite because it  can do a few things like it for one  tracks enemies within a certain range  although i'm not sure if each bar  signifies one or two enemies but using  the ddos though it's kind of like a  counter uav but it includes other  gadgets as you can disable the tech your  opponent is probably using against you  an added bonus it fudges up their radar  too when when some other quick notes on  gadgets there is a deployable barricade  which is good if you've got a heavy  weapon like an lmg and you like to mount  it on barriers walls or floors while  providing you some nifty cover like on  the roof in the farm map it can also  protect you from a mine going off if you  happen to time it right loadout crates  are a thing if you played battlefield  2042 the specialist angel brings down a  loadout crate for you and your team as  well same thing here except you know in  the beta we've been playing mainly 6v6  modes and maps and the loadout crate is  honestly useless  considering that you can just swap your  loadout on respawn like what's the point  you need ammo all right we'll use the  scavenger perk or even an ammunition box  gadget or even grabbing a weapon from  your dead enemy's body these are all  better alternatives in my opinion now  this will probably be more useful on  battle maps when you need to get a  launcher out to stop kill streaks but if  you are in a pinch you can always use it  as cover an interesting rainbow six  siege style gadget is the camera which  is good for watching your back or  domination points but it has a few  drawbacks for example spotting enemies  doesn't seem to give you any scorestreak  points like even a little although i can  see some use for the cameras in the  hostage mode i really don't see much  advantage in something like team  deathmatch or domination modes that you  know the vast majority of cod fans will  be playing the camera does give in  audible ping when an enemy passes it so  it is good for watching your back or  letting you know when an enemy team is  approaching say a domination point or  hostage now that's all good for gadgets  but check out some of these nades man  you've got your classics like semtex  frags smokes and it's like getting a  pepperoni pizza you just can't go wrong  with them but may i introduce you to the  [ __ ] drill charge the first  time i encountered the drill charge was  on the wrong end i mean i was minding my  own business on the second floor and  then blew up and only from the killcam  that i see how the drill charge worked  and god it is fun  it can go through normal cover which is  really cool and it's really good at  blowing up rooms with campers you can  even directly drill charge enemy players  and yeah it looks gnarly another really  cool nade are the shock sticks destiny  fans that use lightning grenades might  recognize the way shock sticks work  for starters they're able to stick on  any surface like a trip mine and will  keep shooting out bolts of electricity  ready to zap anyone even you within  range you can shoot one if they get  thrown at you i mean i like to use them  as a defense measure giving me time to  escape but they're also really great for  preventing enemies from pushing up on  you if you are weak however i have seen  countless teammates use them to breach a  certain point  anyone that gets shocked will have their  fingers seized up on the trigger firing  wildly which is a neat touch the  progression of weapon unlocks is both  easy but it's also confusing as hell not  sure how much of this will change post  beta but i did find that i was unlocking  a boatload of attachments at the end of  a good game and quickly mastering and  unlocking weapon archetypes within a few  hours at most sometimes as fast as a  couple rounds even the problem though  unlocking weapons is confusing because  there's no rhyme or reason and the ui is  just so cluttered it's easy to get lost  so here's a quick explainer there are  new weapon parts known as receivers  which are the base of a certain  archetype like an lmg smg and so on  certain attachments that you unlock are  universal and can be carried over to  other receivers this helps take out the  annoyance of having to grind to unlock  the same red dot side or barrel over and  over again the problem that progression  tree doesn't always make sense if you go  to the progress bar at the top near the  gunsmith you will notice that to unlock  the m16 for example you have to get  progress on the m4 which okay fair  enough but then a  lmg  what  or you know take the hurricane smg for  example an incredibly dominant early  metagun in my opinion that shines  particularly in hip-fire situations but  you know it's an excellent all-arounder  type gun so you want it right and to  unlock the hurricane you have to spend  painful rounds messing not with other  smgs or even an ar but an awful first  fire battle rifle of sorts it just  doesn't make sense so viewers beware  keep an extra eye out on the progression  tabs if there is a gun down the line  that you're hoping to unlock sooner  because it is not as natural or  intuitive as you might hope  now a few things to keep in mind while  you're shooting specifically if you've  got a heavy lmg or another weapon with a  high capacity mag in your hands  normally you could reload cancel by  swapping to a secondary if you're in a  dire situation but that's not the case  here if you start a reload and then swap  to your sidearm and eventually swap back  you will just pick up at the old  animation something to consider for sure  if you know your weapon reload will take  several seconds oh and some thermal  sides still see through smoke from smoke  grenades which is  i mean kind of scummy but oh so  effective to shoot enemies that can't  see you back you know modern warfare 2  does have some pretty neat qol stuff  added to the fray as well  you've got some wicked cool execution  animations if you sneak up on an enemy  but the animations actually change  depending on if your enemy is  self-reviving or not  i've been on the receiving end of being  strangled to death from an execution so  you'll have to take my word for it  ps5 and even ps4 pro players have an fov  slider which is really nifty so i'm  confident we can expect the same for our  xbox gamers in the comments  fov sliders are a good thing and as a pc  main myself it does go a long way in  affecting my gameplay some other quick  notes is that there's a pretty solid ttk  not too fast not too haloey you can  escape properly if you disengage and the  6v6 map so far offers some pretty  interesting engagements on both high and  low vantage points the perk packages  mean you don't have to sacrifice your  kill streaks for specialist boons and  with the weightier grounded guns every  engagement feels exciting  this being an infinity ward game every  map has tons of climbing routes and  areas or angles that you can learn to  use you know i mentioned execution  animations earlier but there's even  other fun attention to detail moments  like swapping to a pistol from the  hurricane smg and doesn't stow away the  gun entirely you actually still hold the  smg in your left hand so you can do your  best rambo impersonation so cod now has  a third person mode which will break  down the why of it all later but what  you do need to know now is that it is  not really a true third person mode  because you can still ads at any time  and it goes back into the traditional  first person perspective but that being  said there are some neat advantages that  you should be mindful of for example in  destiny people would always equip swords  in pvp so it would take them out to a  third person perspective letting them  peek around walls without actually  poking out into the line of fire  three-peaking as we called it kind of  works here too you can scout out some  danger zones without actually being in  danger unless you know someone drill  charges you but still beyond that a lot  of the combat kind of feels the same  besides the odd perspective shift from  third to first person whenever you aim  if you were wondering how to shoulder  swap on my default controls it was  simply clicking down the sticks you  should definitely take advantage of this  because if you don't shoulder swap you  are at a massive disadvantage on every  left-hand corner because the camera by  default sits over your right shoulder  meaning you have to rotate your  character much further to see around  you know i mean aside from a pretty  crummy ui and the unnecessary  third-person mode which we'll get into  later in another video and all that  confusing progression  i have to say that personally i'm  actually having a blast with modern  warfare 2's beta so far and i hope you  will too stay tuned to gamespot as aaron  samson jake decker and myself are going  to be diving into modern warfare hard  we've got some excellent videos cooking  up for you all including a proper  in-depth post-mortem on all the good the  bad and the ugly from that open beta if  you see me in the lobby on ps5 xbox or  pc say what's up  until next time  [Music]  you

